odule/trackback/\">\n    <rdf:Description\n        rdf:about=\"/abs/2607.25530\"\n        dc:identifier=\"/abs/2607.25530\"\n        dc:title=\"Finding the noise: Zero-shot AI Music Detection\"\n        trackback:ping=\"/trackback/2607.25530\" />\n    </rdf:RDF>\n--><div id=\"abs-outer\">\n\n  <div class=\"leftcolumn\">\n    <div class=\"subheader\">\n      <h1>Computer Science > Sound</h1>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"header-breadcrumbs-mobile\">\n      <strong>arXiv:2607.25530v1</strong> (cs)\n    </div>\n<link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"/static/base/1.0.1/css/abs.css\">\n<div id=\"content-inner\">\n  <div id=\"abs\">\n    <div class=\"dateline\">\n  [Submitted on 28 Jul 2026]</div>\n    <h1 class=\"title mathjax\"><span class=\"descriptor\">Title:</span>Finding the noise: Zero-shot AI Music Detection</h1>\n    <div class=\"authors\"><span class=\"descriptor\">Authors:</span><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Afchar,+D\" rel=\"nofollow\">Darius Afchar</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Hennequin,+R\" rel=\"nofollow\">Romain Hennequin</a></div>            <div id=\"download-button-info\" hidden>View a PDF of the paper titled Finding the noise: Zero-shot AI Music Detection, by Darius Afchar and Romain Hennequin</div>\n    <a class=\"mobile-submission-download\" href=\"/pdf/2607.25530v1\">View PDF</a>\n    <a class=\"mobile-submission-download\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2607.25530v1\">HTML (experimental)</a>\n\n\n\n    <blockquote class=\"abstract mathjax\">\n            <span class=\"descriptor\">Abstract:</span>We present a novel method for AI-generated music detection in scenarios where the models that generated the input samples are unknown to the detector (e.g., from a newly released service). Since 2023, there has been a multiplication of user-friendly AI-music generation services (e.g., Suno, Udio), along with regular updates and new features. There is thus a need to address synthetic content detection in an unsupervised way to adapt to this rapidly changing context. This angle has not been much studied in music yet. We propose to study two tasks. First, discriminating between real and synthetic music. This may be approached in a one-class manner, namely, using some baseline real music and trying to determine what falls outside. Second, zero-shot multi-class identification, which is more similar to an unsupervised clustering task on a mix of real and various AI-music generations, where the goal is to create coherent, high-purity clusters. We propose a combination of a previously proposed artifact-extraction method, on top of which we apply non-negative matrix factorization and simple classification and clustering methods. We achieve excellent performance on both tasks, showing that the proposed methods may be used to monitor large-scale catalogs that may receive AI-generated samples from various newly released generative models.\n    </blockquote>\n\n    <!--CONTEXT-->\n    <div class=\"metatable\">\n      <table summary=\"Additional metadata\">        <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Comments:</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell comments mathjax\">preprint -- may be modified for a future publication</td>\n        </tr>\n<tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Subjects:</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell subjects\">\n            <span class=\"primary-subject\">Sound (cs.SD)</span></td>\n        </tr><tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Cite as:</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxivid\"><span class=\"arxivid\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.25530\">arXiv:2607.25530</a> [cs.SD]</span></td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">&nbsp;</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxividv\">(or <span class=\"arxivid\">\n              <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.25530v1\">arXiv:2607.25530v1</a> [cs.SD]</span> for this version)\n          </td>\n        </tr>\n        <tr>\n          <td class=\"tablecell label\">&nbsp;</td>\n          <td class=\"tablecell arxivdoi\">              <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2607.25530\" id=\"arxiv-doi-link\">https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2607.25530</a><div class=\"button-and-tooltip\">\n              <button class=\"more-info\" aria-describedby=\"more-info-desc-1\">\n                <svg height=\"15\" role=\"presentation\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\"><path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M256 8C119.043 8 8 119.083 8 256c0 136.997 111.043 248 248 248s248-111.003 248-248C504 119.083 392.957 8 256 8zm0 110c23.196 0 42 18.804 42 42s-18.804 42-42 42-42-18.804-42-42 18.804-42 42-42zm56 254c0 6.627-5.373 12-12 12h-88c-6.627 0-12-5.373-12-12v-24c0-6.627 5.373-12 12-12h12v-64h-12c-6.627 0-12-5.373-12-12v-24c0-6.627 5.373-12 12-12h64c6.627 0 12 5.373 12 12v100h12c6.627 0 12 5.373 12 12v24z\" class=\"\"></path></svg>\n                <span class=\"visually-hidden\">Focus to learn more</span>\n              </button>\n              <!-- tooltip description -->\n              <div role=\"tooltip\" id=\"more-info-desc-1\">\n                <span class=\"left-corner\"></span>                  arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite (pending registration)</div>\n            </div>\n          </td>\n        </tr></table>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n    <div class=\"submission-history\">\n      <h2>Submission history</h2> From: Darius Afchar [<a href=\"/show-email/82a32d0f/2607.25530\" rel=\"nofollow\">view email</a>]      <br/>    <strong>[v1]</strong>\n        Tue, 28 Jul 2026 10:17:35 UTC (2,816 KB)<br/>\n</div>\n  </div>\n  <!--end leftcolumn-->\n<div class=\"extra-services\">    <div class=\"full-text\">\n      <a name=\"other\"></a>\n      <span class=\"descriptor\">Full-text links:</span>\n      <h2>Access Paper:</h2>\n      <ul>\n  <div id=\"download-button-info\" hidden>\nView a PDF of the paper titled Finding the noise: Zero-shot AI Music Detection, by Darius